course: dictionary
lesson: 5213
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning is meant. Java is a good example. It can be an island, a kind of coffee, or a computer language.
explain: «Minecraft was first written in Java; the Bedrock edition is written in C++.» Here Java is not a place or a drink. The clues are written and edition, which tell you it is a programming language used to make a game.
explain: «JavaScript and Java are different languages despite the similar names.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. Languages and names tell you that Java is a programming language, not a drink.
fact: Java is a large island in Indonesia, where the capital city Jakarta is.
fact: Java is also a programming language used to make apps and programs.
fact: In American slang, «a cup of java» means coffee.
fact: A kind of coffee is grown on the island of Java, so it is called Java coffee.
fact: JavaScript is a different language from Java, even though the names are similar.
exercise: «Minecraft was first written in Java.» In this sentence, Java means what? | *A computer programming language | An island in Indonesia | A kind of tree | A cup of coffee
exercise: Americans say «a cup of java» in a café. What does java mean here? | A computer game | A kind of bread | *Coffee | A large island
exercise: Which fact is about the island of Java? | It is a website that runs games | *Jakarta is its capital city, and it is in Indonesia | It is a drink people order in America | It is a language used to build apps
test: In «JavaScript and Java are different languages despite the similar names», what kind of word is Java? | An island | *A programming language | A country | Coffee
test: What does «the island of Java» tell you about Java? | A city in America | A computer language | *A large island, part of Indonesia | Coffee
exam: Which meaning of java fits best in «Minecraft was first written in Java»? | *A programming language | A capital city called Jakarta | A cup of coffee | An island in Indonesia
